  "scope_details": [
    "Actual Original Django/psycopg and native SQLx invoke the same owned copiedDB functions. SQLSTATE/message/detail/hint/context/position fields and rendered exception argument strings compare exactly for35cases.",
    "P0001 only, cursor/internal positions rejected, each diagnostic field/output bounded8KiB. No mapping of everyDatabaseError to ProgrammingError.",
    "Source spacing is two spaces after diagnostic labels. Present empty DETAIL/HINT remains a label; absent fields are omitted. Nested/multiline context and interior whitespace remain exact.",
    "Final stripping uses the observed Python3.13 whitespace set:22 control/Unicode boundaries include U+001C\u2013001F while U+180E/U+FEFF remain. This formats existing diagnostic data; it does not generate Python stack frames.",
    "No service/cause changes were required: caller can borrow SQLxPgDatabaseError from the preserved owned StoreError. No new graph edge was needed; module is cfgtest only."
  ],
  "remaining_gates": [
    "Adopt bounded formatter in separately tested known-raised classifier after detailed stage/commit/physical release API/resource gates.",
    "No generic SQLSTATEs, cursor/caret/internalQUERY rendering, otherlocale/PostgreSQL/driver versions or arbitrary oversized errors are accepted.",
    "Native diagnostic traceback policy, terminal-result worker attachment, exact type/args/state/TTL/lock effects and parented/ETA exceptions remain separate gates."
  ],
